   "body": "·/·r·elease cloud/i1038-sonnet\n\nHand-off (operator asked to write everything down; the orchestrator lost the link). **Where it stands: PR #1131, draft, on hold for a Mac measurement.**\n\n- **PR:** #1131, head `121ecf717901f18b2e57639323fb9ad7ab1aeb74`, draft, labels `compile-check` and `experimental`. Opus 5.5 APPROVE on that head (round 3, delta), verdicts posted. The Compile check was last seen green on an earlier head (`37f1cb76`); **I never saw it on `121ecf71`**. Nothing has been run locally (Linux, no Xcode).\n- **What the PR does:** (B) « MP multiples → dark topic » is a plain `ExperimentalFeatureRow` with its ⓘ; `DescribedFeatureRow`, `showsExplanationUnderSwitch` and their markers are removed; (A) one constant, `SettingsRowSpacing.titleToDescription = 6` pt, read by `ExperimentalFeatureRow` and `MPStorageSettingsRows`.\n- **What is NOT settled (A):** the operator first said « 6 pt is right » then corrected through the orchestrator: the reference is **today's rendered gap of the « MP multiples → dark topic » row**, which must be reproduced for every row, measured on a device or simulator, not guessed from code constants. From the code, today's MP row is `VStack(spacing: 2){ Toggle; Text(.footnote) }` (see `git show origin/dev-swift:App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/MPDarkTopic/DescribedFeatureRow.swift`) and `ExperimentalFeatureRow` is `VStack(spacing: 6){ HStack{ Toggle; ⓘ }; Text }`, which says the ⓘ rows have the **larger** gap: the opposite of « they look cramped », so a constant is not the whole story (the toggle's own row height, the ⓘ button and the Form row padding enter the rendered gap).\n- **What is left:**\n  1. mac/M1 measures, on `origin/dev-swift` (before #1131): the vertical distance from the switch title's baseline (or the switch's vertical centre) to the description's first-line top, in points, for the MP row and for another row with its ⓘ open (one iPhone, one text size). I asked for this on #893 through the orchestrator; the numbers were to land on #1131.\n  2. Set `SettingsRowSpacing.titleToDescription` (and an offset if the ⓘ row's toggle is taller) from the two numbers, and add an app-hosted test that reads the y positions of both row shapes.\n  3. Opus delta review, Compile check green, ready line on #893, merge, close with `Done in #1131 (merged as <sha>)`.\n- **Ledger in the PR body** (GAP-903 `gap-edit` and a `ledger-note` for CHANGELOG row 1042) is valid (`ledger.py check-body`). MP storage's state line goes from 2 to 6 pt on this branch: list it in the device check.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
